# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings.
#
# The site is edited on Windows and served from Linux, and without this Git
# warns on every one of the ~140 text files in the repository and can show a
# whole clean checkout as modified on the other machine.
#
# `text=auto` stores LF in the repository and checks out whatever the platform
# uses. Nothing the browser reads cares either way.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The exceptions, and why.
#
# legacy_index.html is the original site's home page, kept as the REFERENCE
# for what the old site emitted. It carries exactly one deliberate edit — a
# `robots` noindex tag, README §10 — and is otherwise as supplied, LF endings
# included. Normalising those endings would rewrite all 314 of them and change
# every line of a file whose whole value is being the record of what the old
# site sent, so it is stored byte-for-byte as it sits on disk.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
legacy_index.html -text

# Binary assets: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.JPG  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.rar  binary
*.zip  binary
*.pdf  binary

# Vendored Three.js: not this project's source, and a diff of it helps nobody.
assets/vendor/three/** linguist-vendored

# So GitHub's language stats describe the site rather than the reference copy
# of the old home page.
legacy_index.html linguist-vendored
